  "summary": "The handbook describes that the high‑pressure compressor is inspected by removing the inlet screen, cleaning the inducer, illuminating the vanes, rotating the compressor to view each vane for cracks (especially leading edges), and using magnetic‑particle or fluorescent‑penetrant inspection on repaired blades.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Inspection of the compressor inducer requires removing the air‑inlet screen, cleaning the inducer, and inspecting it with a strong light while slowly turning the compressor to check each vane for cracks, especially in the leading edges.",
      "citations": [1]
    },
    {
      "text": "Repaired compressor blades are inspected by magnetic‑particle or fluorescent‑penetrant inspection methods to ensure all damage traces have been removed.",
      "citations": [1]
